ong-term win on border  security for the president and the  administration there is still that  possibility it is possible that without  the pressure of government being shut  down and all the problems that caused  without that pressure perhaps people  could take a more sober look at the  president's last proposal which in  addition to money for a boarder barrier  included all sorts of things that both  party likes more technology to detect  drugs at ports of entry humanitarian aid  more beds at the detention centers more  immigration judges all the sorts of  things that were part of a package that  both parties  in the past prior to Trump would  actually support and that would include  a physical barrier at the border always  part of that so perhaps it's possible  that when all the craziness of the  shutdown is over people could take  another look at that proposal Josh we're  hearing from our producer up on Capitol  Hill chat program that too soon to do  the State of the Union on Tuesday they  believe but they're floating February  5th clearly the president wanted to  deliver the State of the Union address  in the House chamber with all the pomp  and circumstance look the State of the  Union whenever it's scheduled is going  to be president Trump's opportunity to  get some political momentum back and  took to Byron's point Republicans win  the immigration argument when it's  broadly about border security it's when  Trump kind of got caught up in the wall  we need to have this for the wall that  really put him and the Republicans in  Congress in a corner and even he backed  off from that you know saying it was  really just four steel slats or four a  combination of border security measures  Trump needs to reset his immigration  agenda his border security agenda with  the State of the Union but he has to  think more broadly he can't just be  speaking to the the 30% 35% base he has  to look at the broad majority of the  country that does want solid border  enforcement in the meantime Matthew  Democrats are relishing the fact that  they're tweaking the president with  Nancy Pelosi suggesting that she's the  big winner here you have representative  Karen bass tweeting out that speaker  Pelosi should give the State of the  Union address and she's obviously the  one running the country well Karen bass  is wrong the president is still the  president he has all the powers of the  office you look at some of the things  he's done on foreign policy for example  you see the immense power of the  presidency Nancy Pelosi is an extremely  savvy legislator and she knew she had a  winning hand especially when President  Trump in December said that he would  take the credit or blame if the  government shut down well that's what  happened and the public listened to  President Trump and they blamed him but  now I think is an opportunity to try to  not only reset the immigration debate as  Josh said they really start thinking  seriously and strategically about what  it will take to expand his support to  get win him reelection in 2020  all right gentlemen thank you we'll see  you later in the show
 

